### What happens?

`duckdb_v2_value_get_uint` on a value of ENUM type returns uninitialized memory and reports `DUCKDB_V2_ERROR_NONE`. 

Every enum member returns same value with run, but value differs between runs. 

```
run 1: returned 603994400, 603994400, 603994400
run 2: returned 738212576, 738212576, 738212576
run 3: returned 4093656016, 4093656016, 4093656016
run 4: returned 2885698112, 2885698112, 2885698112
```

Those are `'sad'::mood`, `'ok'::mood` and `'happy'::mood` of
`CREATE TYPE mood AS ENUM ('sad', 'ok', 'happy')`, read one after another in a single process.

The same conversion through SQL fails cleanly, so the C API and the engine disagree:

```
D SELECT 'sad'::mood::UINTEGER;
Conversion Error: Could not convert string 'sad' to UINT32
```



### To Reproduce

The patch below adds a test case to `test/api/capi/v2/test_capi_v2_value.cpp`. 

It reads three different enum members and asserts only that they are not all the same value


```
test/api/capi/v2/test_capi_v2_value.cpp:1612: FAILED:
  REQUIRE( read[0] != read[1] )
with expansion:
  603994400 (0x24003920)
  !=
  603994400 (0x24003920)
with message:
  returned 603994400, 603994400, 603994400
```

* The assertion is guarded on all three calls returning success

```diff
diff --git a/test/api/capi/v2/test_capi_v2_value.cpp b/test/api/capi/v2/test_capi_v2_value.cpp
index 259b51451d..4e73568464 100644
--- a/test/api/capi/v2/test_capi_v2_value.cpp
+++ b/test/api/capi/v2/test_capi_v2_value.cpp
@@ -1580,6 +1580,40 @@ TEST_CASE("V2: value_cast null-arg refusals", "[capi_v2][value][cast]") {
 // unwrapping getter -- the cast machinery is the whole access path.
 // ===========================================================================

+TEST_CASE("V2: value_get_uint on an ENUM does not report a constant", "[capi_v2][value][typed]") {
+	EnvFixture f;
+	QueryResult r;
+	ExecSQL(f.conn, "CREATE TYPE mood AS ENUM ('sad', 'ok', 'happy')");
+	REQUIRE(Query(f.conn, "SELECT 'sad'::mood AS a, 'ok'::mood AS b, 'happy'::mood AS c", &r) ==
+	        DUCKDB_V2_ERROR_NONE);
+	auto chunk = StepChunk(r);
+	REQUIRE(chunk != nullptr);
+
+	std::vector<uint32_t> read;
+	std::vector<DUCKDB_V2_ERROR> codes;
+	for (idx_t col = 0; col < 3; col++) {
+		duckdb_v2_vector_handle vec = nullptr;
+		REQUIRE(duckdb_v2_data_chunk_get_vector(chunk, col, &vec, nullptr) == DUCKDB_V2_ERROR_NONE);
+		duckdb_v2_value_handle cell = nullptr;
+		REQUIRE(duckdb_v2_vector_get_value(vec, 0, &cell, nullptr) == DUCKDB_V2_ERROR_NONE);
+		uint32_t out = 0;
+		codes.push_back(duckdb_v2_value_get_uint(cell, &out, nullptr));
+		read.push_back(out);
+		duckdb_v2_value_destroy(&cell);
+	}
+	duckdb_v2_data_chunk_destroy(&chunk);
+
+	// Three different members of enum. Either reports ordinals, or it fails.
+	// Reporting one constant for all three, with success code, is neither.
+	INFO("returned " << read[0] << ", " << read[1] << ", " << read[2]);
+	const bool all_succeeded = codes[0] == DUCKDB_V2_ERROR_NONE && codes[1] == DUCKDB_V2_ERROR_NONE &&
+	                           codes[2] == DUCKDB_V2_ERROR_NONE;
+	if (all_succeeded) {
+		REQUIRE(read[0] != read[1]);
+		REQUIRE(read[1] != read[2]);
+	}
+}
+
 TEST_CASE("V2: VARIANT cells are read by casting them", "[capi_v2][value][variant]") {
 	EnvFixture f;
 	QueryResult r;
```

