### What happens?

v2 C API: A table function registered is scanned by **one task** whenever query returns rows, however many threads it declares. The same registration is scanned in parallel for an aggregate, and in parallel again once `preserve_insertion_order=false` is set.

The v2 C API exposes no way to supply a batch index, so a C API consumer cannot opt out of the serial path.

## Impact


DuckDB creates one local state per task. Counting `init_local` callbacks counts tasks with no timing involved. 

Same registration, same query, same data, 32-thread scheduler. Timings below come from attached reproducer probe scaled to 8.4M rows varying the thread count; the test as attached keeps 64 rows and `max_threads` 4.

| declared `max_threads` | query | tasks | time |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 16 | `SELECT * FROM par_probe()` | **1** | 24.0 ms |
| 16 | same, `preserve_insertion_order=false` | 16 | 6.4 ms |
| 4 | `SELECT * FROM par_probe()` | **1** | 30.6 ms |
| 4 | same, `preserve_insertion_order=false` | 4 | 11.2 ms |

Declaring more threads changes nothing: the row-returning query gets one task at `max_threads` 4 and 16

`SET preserve_insertion_order=false` recovers the parallelism but changes query semantics

## The gap

`TableFunction::get_partition_data` is what makes a scan eligible to stay ordered while running in
parallel. Every table function DuckDB ships for bulk data sets it:

| scan | sets `get_partition_data` | parallel for row-returning queries |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `table_scan` ([:1034](https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb/blob/625f75fce87c7b49c0bef7c331bd89a32d1c0d38/src/function/table/table_scan.cpp#L1034)) | yes | yes |
| `arrow_scan` ([:341](https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb/blob/625f75fce87c7b49c0bef7c331bd89a32d1c0d38/src/function/table/arrow.cpp#L341)) | yes | yes |
| multi-file reader, parquet and CSV ([:91](https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb/blob/625f75fce87c7b49c0bef7c331bd89a32d1c0d38/src/include/duckdb/common/multi_file/multi_file_function.hpp#L91)) | yes | yes |
| a v2 C API table function | **cannot** | **no** |

`duckdb_v2.h` has no partition or batch-index entry point.
[`capi_v2_func_table.cpp`](https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb/blob/625f75fce87c7b49c0bef7c331bd89a32d1c0d38/src/main/capi/v2/capi_v2_func_table.cpp#L477-L492) wires `cardinality`, `table_scan_progress`, `pushdown_complex_filter` and `projection_pushdown`, and
has nothing to wire here.

## Explanation / Analysis

#### `PhysicalTableScan::SupportsPartitioning` returns false without `get_partition_data`
https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb/blob/625f75fce87c7b49c0bef7c331bd89a32d1c0d38/src/execution/operator/scan/physical_table_scan.cpp#L249-L255

#### so `AllSourcesSupportBatchIndex` is false
https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb/blob/625f75fce87c7b49c0bef7c331bd89a32d1c0d38/src/execution/physical_operator.cpp#L298-L306

#### so `UseBatchIndex` is false, and the collector picks `ResultOrdering::SOURCE_ORDERED`
https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb/blob/625f75fce87c7b49c0bef7c331bd89a32d1c0d38/src/execution/operator/helper/physical_result_collector.cpp#L23-L37

#### and `PhysicalResultSink::ParallelSink()` returns false for it
https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb/blob/625f75fce87c7b49c0bef7c331bd89a32d1c0d38/src/execution/operator/helper/physical_result_sink.cpp#L269-L272

> `// Source order is preserved by keeping the sink single-threaded`

An aggregate doesn't enter chain: `PreserveInsertionOrder` returns false for a plan that does not preserve order: why `preserve_insertion_order=false` restores parallelism.



### To Reproduce

Test case in `test/api/capi/v2/test_capi_v2_table_function.cpp`, plus`par_probe()` table function that counts `init_local` calls. 

The aggregate arm and the `preserve_insertion_order=false` arm pass. The row-returning arm fails:

```
test/api/capi/v2/test_capi_v2_table_function.cpp:759: FAILED:
  REQUIRE( rows_tasks > 1 )
with expansion:
  1 > 1
```

```diff
diff --git a/test/api/capi/v2/test_capi_v2_table_function.cpp b/test/api/capi/v2/test_capi_v2_table_function.cpp
index 99010aaa53..7d3860e55b 100644
--- a/test/api/capi/v2/test_capi_v2_table_function.cpp
+++ b/test/api/capi/v2/test_capi_v2_table_function.cpp
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 #include "test_capi_v2.hpp"

+#include <atomic>
 #include <cstring>

 // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
@@ -494,6 +495,75 @@ void StateExecCb(duckdb_v2_table_function_exec_info_handle info, duckdb_v2_conte
 	duckdb_v2_vector_set_size(vec, produced, err);
 }

+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+// par_probe(): a trivial source whose job is to be scanned. DuckDB creates one local state
+// per task, counting init_local calls counts tasks with no timing
+std::atomic<idx_t> par_tasks {0};
+struct ParGlobal {
+	std::atomic<idx_t> remaining {64};
+};
+
+void ParBindCb(duckdb_v2_table_function_bind_info_handle info, duckdb_v2_context_handle context,
